    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated the three separate duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into a single derived `identityKey` on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**The key** \u2014 added `Owner.getIdentityKey()` returning `normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + (email or empty) + \"|\" + (householdId or empty)`. Telephone and email are already stored normalized (E.164 / lower-cased) and `householdId` is null unless the owner belongs to a shared household.\n\n**New behaviour** \u2014 `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` scans existing owners and throws `OwnerIdentityConflictException` (\u2192 409, body `{\"errors\":[\"identityKey\"]}`) **only when the new owner's whole identityKey exactly equals an existing owner's**. Because telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have different keys and are both allowed \u2014 a genuine behaviour change from the old household check.\n\n**Pipeline** (`owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 removed `checkTelephoneUnique`/`checkEmailUnique`/`checkHouseholdUnique` and inserted `checkIdentityUnique` **after** `assignHousehold`, so the new owner already carries any assigned `householdId` when its key is compared (this also correctly catches exact re-registration of a household member \u2014 a case the old field-by-field checks running before assignment would have missed).\n\n**Return** \u2014 added a read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` (DTOs are generated from it); MapStruct auto-maps it from `getIdentityKey()`, so it's returned in owner responses.\n\n**Cleanup** \u2014 deleted the three obsolete `CheckOwner*Unique` functions, the three conflict exceptions + handlers, and their escalation YAMLs; updated `AssignHousehold` and the `sharesHousehold`/`householdId` descriptions to reflect that duplicate detection now flows solely through the identityKey. `sharesHousehold` remains meaningful for linking household members but no longer gates duplicate rejection.\n\nThe new `coreRejectsIdentityCollision` test (second owner reusing the first's telephone \u2192 409) passes, and the full suite is green.",
